ous round (Round 0). This suggests possible weakness, but we are in early position and need to build the pot carefully.  \n- Raising to 200 or higher helps build initiative and leverages your position and chip lead. Given your hand's potential to make straights and top pair, a moderate raise is attractive.  \n- Going all-in (-2) is overly aggressive pre-flop with this hand, especially when you're in the lead and don’t need to risk your stack unnecessarily. It would only make sense if you were short-stacked or reading extreme weakness, which isn't indicated.\n\nReason:  \nJack-Ten offsuit is a speculative but strong enough hand to raise for value and initiative, especially from a winning position. Since the opponent showed passivity last round (checking), it makes sense to take control of the pot now. A minimum raise of 200 chips is sufficient to build the pot without overcommitting.\n\nAnswer: 200"}
